list.item:
Tramadol hydrochloride tablets are contraindicated for post-operative management in pediatric patients younger than    18 years    of    age    following    tonsillectomy    and/or    adenoidectomy    [see
                                 Contraindications (4)
                              ].

As with adults, when prescribing opioids for adolescents, healthcare providers should choose the lowest effective dose for the shortest period of time and inform patients and caregivers about these risks and the signs of opioid overdose [see
                                 Use in Specific Populations (8.4), Overdosage (10)
                              ].
